Both of them belong to the Khyentse lineage.

38
00:06:03,065 --> 00:06:17,316
Both of them are the reincarnation of the first Jamyang Khyentse Rinpoche, one of the founders of the Rimé tradition in Tibet, which is a non-sectarian tradition.

39
00:06:17,416 --> 00:06:19,257
The Khyentse is the founder of the non-sectarian tradition.

40
00:06:20,718 --> 00:06:25,222
So therefore, Khyentse Rinpoche has a connection with many spiritual masters,

41
00:06:26,937 --> 00:06:34,281
I think it's hardly we can find any spiritual master who is not somehow connected with Khyentse Rinpoche.

42
00:06:36,322 --> 00:06:43,066
So that is one very, very great quality among many, many special qualities.

43
00:06:43,406 --> 00:06:51,671
So being so loved and cared by Khyentse Rinpoche and then many great teachers also being very, very kind to me.

44
00:06:52,691 --> 00:06:54,292
So I took a great opportunity.

45
00:06:55,345 --> 00:06:58,087
to meet all those great masters.

46
00:07:01,869 --> 00:07:13,016
So Khyentse Rinpoche, Dilgo Khyentse Rinpoche, also, how he become what he is, how he become what he is.

47
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:23,622
Also, he was,  Dilgo Khyentse Rinpoche was, he was born to a noble family,

48
00:07:27,223 --> 00:07:34,766
and very devoted to Dharma, one of the main benefactors of Jamyang Mipham Rinpoche.

49
00:07:34,806 --> 00:07:39,307
So many of you might know one of the greatest Tibetan scholar.

50
00:07:40,988 --> 00:07:54,452
So when Khentsey Rinpoche was born to this family, actually many lamas want to recognize Khentsey Rinpoche as their reincarnation of their teacher.

51
00:07:57,086 --> 00:08:04,228
So, but Khentsey Rinpoche's father wanted Khentsey Rinpoche to continue his family legacy.

52
00:08:04,968 --> 00:08:14,151
So he doesn't want to accept that his son is going to become a spiritual master, not carry on the family legacy.

53
00:08:16,292 --> 00:08:26,075
So he said, of course, not to the lamas, but he told anybody, because that time is quite powerful, one of those kinds of laws, even in the English.

54
00:08:26,833 --> 00:08:32,094
Anybody who says my son is a reincarnation of a Lama, I'm going to whip them a hundred times.

55
00:08:34,255 --> 00:08:38,616
So people didn't dare to say, talk much.

56
00:08:40,376 --> 00:08:45,718
So one of his, one of Khyentse Rinpoche's father's root guru is also Shechen Gyaltsab Rinpoche.

57
00:08:48,438 --> 00:08:52,199
We have so many names, so I try to minimize the names instead of confusing you.

58
00:08:53,079 --> 00:08:55,180
So one of the teachers, Shechen Gyaltsab, so he really

59
00:08:56,153 --> 00:08:57,314
have faith in Shechen Gyaltsab.

60
00:08:57,634 --> 00:09:07,578
So Gyaltsab Rinpoche said, OK, now he is reincarnation of Khentsey, so you must let him practice dharma, join the monastery.

61
00:09:09,619 --> 00:09:14,221
Then he also not easily, he didn't let Khentsey go easily.

62
00:09:15,462 --> 00:09:18,703
He said, I need a proof, kind of proof that he is reincarnation.

63
00:09:19,583 --> 00:09:25,546
So until Gyaltsab Rinpoche really told him how he knew he was reincarnation, his father would not accept.

64
00:09:26,467 --> 00:09:41,439
So Gyaltsab Rinpoche said, last night one of the protector came, I think particularly Tsering Ma, belongs to Longchen Nyingtik tradition, protector came and told me personally that he will benefit the Dharma, so we have to let him go.

65
00:09:41,879 --> 00:09:48,785
But still father a little bit hesitant and so I don't want to go into so detail, but then Gyaltsab Rinpoche had an accident and he

66
00:09:49,521 --> 00:10:04,029
He almost died, and then they did a divination council with many, many teachers, and everybody says, if you don't let him be what he is, he will not live, because he's not born to work as a, to carry on your family legacy.

67
00:10:04,409 --> 00:10:17,316
So the father, before Khentsey Rinpoche recover from the accident, he start putting the dharma robes, dharma robes on him, and he said, okay, now, now I'll let you go.

68
00:10:17,656 --> 00:10:18,136
So like that.

69
00:10:20,487 --> 00:10:25,152
So then he let Khentsey Rinpoche go, and then Khentsey Rinpoche met with him.

70
00:10:26,673 --> 00:10:29,316
He went to see his teacher, Shechen Gyaltsab Rinpoche.

71
00:10:29,656 --> 00:10:34,340
And that time, Dzongsar Khyentse, previous Dzongsar Khyentse, was also studying.

72
00:10:34,361 --> 00:10:38,725
So they sort of studied together with Shechen Gyaltsang Rinpoche.

73
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:43,950
So how he became what he is, is that

74
00:10:45,047 --> 00:10:55,595
Rinpoche, one condition, one condition was that Rinpoche had a very, very good tutor, that is his elder brother, who was also a great practitioner, very knowledgeable.

75
00:10:56,335 --> 00:11:09,364
So he knew which lama, which teacher to go and see, which teacher to go to see, which teacher, because at that time there were many great masters living there, so he took to the right teacher.

76
00:11:10,945 --> 00:11:12,887
That is one, I think, reason.

77
00:11:13,587 --> 00:11:14,488
Then second reason,

78
00:11:14,899 --> 00:11:22,505
There's many of these teachers, the great teachers, who think that Khyentse Rinpoche is the reincarnation of their teacher.

79
00:11:24,227 --> 00:11:30,652
So they're very, very happy to give any teaching that he requests, really like special attention to Khyentse Rinpoche.

80
00:11:31,433 --> 00:11:32,774
So that's also one privilege.

81
00:11:33,594 --> 00:11:34,435
Privilege, right?

82
00:11:34,795 --> 00:11:38,178
One of the reasons.

83
00:11:39,319 --> 00:11:41,661
And then, I think another thing is that

84
00:11:43,650 --> 00:11:47,153
The family is quite well off and supportive of Dharma.

85
00:11:47,313 --> 00:11:57,741
So whenever Rinpoche wants to go and receive teachings or study with Lamas, they always support him with sending grains, Sambha and all those supportings.

86
00:11:57,761 --> 00:12:01,204
So Rinpoche had all his family support for him to do that.

87
00:12:05,367 --> 00:12:08,730
Then on top of that, his own kind of determination.

88
00:12:10,134 --> 00:12:12,455
He studied with so many different teachers.

89
00:12:12,515 --> 00:12:17,236
He used to say he has like 50 different teachers from all different schools.

90
00:12:18,757 --> 00:12:24,859
And together he spent like 20 years in retreat practice.

91
00:12:25,359 --> 00:12:31,721
So all those conditions together, then you can say he became who he is.

92
00:12:34,242 --> 00:12:39,504
So it's not kind of a title that you say, okay, you are a high Lama and he suddenly becomes high Lama.

93
00:12:40,279 --> 00:12:41,420
is not like that.

94
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:56,672
I think even to become Khentsey Rinpoche and how he became he is, it's a great example for us that is in a path how we have to progress to get to some kind of higher realization.

95
00:12:57,592 --> 00:13:09,722
So in Khentsey Rinpoche's case, there are many, many circumstances that came together which became what he is.

96
00:13:12,318 --> 00:13:22,826
So then there are a lot of stories or signs of his accomplishment in Tibet.

97
00:13:23,967 --> 00:13:28,470
So a few of these stories that I'd like to share.

98
00:13:30,492 --> 00:13:33,134
Because there's only four words, so I better add some stories.

99
00:13:40,162 --> 00:13:48,889
If you look at all his writings, what we have just now is like 25 volumes of his writings.

100
00:13:49,509 --> 00:13:58,476
That is knowledge, from that we can learn, which is knowledge.

101
00:13:59,737 --> 00:14:06,362
And then spending 20 years in retreat, from that we can know how much practice he has done.

102
00:14:07,443 --> 00:14:09,565
And relying upon 50 different teachers,

103
00:14:10,513 --> 00:14:19,722
and how much he sort of received teachings, and he received almost all kind of lineage, non-stop.

104
00:14:22,364 --> 00:14:35,777
And then teachings that he get, the big, big teachings, which takes about six months to give the whole cycle, so he gave them three times, and then

105
00:14:37,976 --> 00:14:43,040
The works he has done since he came out of Tibet, the building monasteries, reprinting books.

106
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:47,983
So it looks like one man lived many lives, many lives.

107
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:52,266
If you look at his works, he did nothing but writing books.

108
00:14:52,947 --> 00:14:55,549
If you look at his teachings, he did nothing but giving teachings.

109
00:14:56,249 --> 00:14:58,611
If you look at his practice, he did nothing but practice.

110
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:06,657
So like many kind of people's kind of work in one.

111
00:15:07,055 --> 00:15:11,699
So, all those things put together, then it becomes what he is.

112
00:15:13,861 --> 00:15:16,102
Then some of the stories were quite funny.

113
00:15:17,644 --> 00:15:21,267
That one time, Khentsey Rinpoche was in Tibet.

114
00:15:21,307 --> 00:15:26,351
He was invited by a nomad compass, eastern Tibet.

115
00:15:26,471 --> 00:15:30,214
They are a little bit like American wild west cowboy, cowboy style.

116
00:15:31,155 --> 00:15:36,239
They like to carry guns and ride horse and wore,

117
00:15:36,833 --> 00:15:38,394
gun, hat, and like that.

118
00:15:39,574 --> 00:15:44,597
So the guns, guns is very important for them, very treasure.

119
00:15:45,877 --> 00:15:47,698
So one family have a very special gun.

120
00:15:48,339 --> 00:15:49,879
Everybody knows about this gun.

121
00:15:51,340 --> 00:16:01,985
So one day, Khentsey Rinpoche came to his tent, yak hair tent, and Rinpoche, Khentsey Rinpoche asked, is this your famous gun that's hanging on the door?

122
00:16:03,086 --> 00:16:03,726
And they said, yes.

123
00:16:04,666 --> 00:16:05,667
And we just took the,

124
00:16:06,735 --> 00:16:10,456
what you call barrel and blow on it, blow blast it and then went.

125
00:16:11,816 --> 00:16:12,556
Then Rinpoche left.

126
00:16:12,916 --> 00:16:15,817
And after that, his gun could never hit anymore.

127
00:16:18,657 --> 00:16:20,498
Always missed the target.

128
00:16:23,398 --> 00:16:25,559
So this story became quite famous.

129
00:16:26,739 --> 00:16:30,680
So whenever Rinpoche went, everybody hide guns.

130
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:36,601
So there are many signs of his accomplishment like that.

131
00:16:38,625 --> 00:16:43,447
And so those are the kind of signs of accomplishment.

132
00:16:45,969 --> 00:17:03,497
And I think one thing in the story that I heard is Rinpoche's last meeting with his teacher, Longtsey Khyentse Rinpoche, was in Tibet and after Longtsey Khyentse came to Sikkim and Khyentse Rinpoche came later.

133
00:17:06,668 --> 00:17:09,210
So Rinpoche never met him after Tibet.

134
00:17:13,293 --> 00:17:33,008
And Rinpoche, sort of, after leaving his home, coming to India, and then passing away of his teacher, and I think Rinpoche felt like sort of hopeless, kind of, hopeless, hopeless situation.

135
00:17:34,849 --> 00:17:35,550
And I heard that

136
00:17:37,290 --> 00:17:47,797
which is sort of like got sick, and some of the photos you can see very, very thin, sort of not much kind of hope for the Buddha Dharma.

137
00:17:47,997 --> 00:17:52,300
Of course, there's nothing much in which he cares, nothing more than the Buddha Dharma.

138
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:56,603
So, seeing teacher passing away, kind of no hope.

139
00:17:58,024 --> 00:18:04,868
And then he came to India, and he met one person who's very close with previous Dzongtsey Khyentse.

140
00:18:06,683 --> 00:18:11,484
And Rinpoche talked with him, and how did Dzongtsey Khyentsey Rinpoche passed away, all that.

141
00:18:11,684 --> 00:18:20,166
And then he told a story to Rinpoche that he met Dzongtsey Khyentsey Choejey Loday Rinpoche before he passed away.

142
00:18:21,046 --> 00:18:27,428
And Dzongtsey Khyentsey Choejey Loday Rinpoche was bedridden, sick in bed, bedridden, bedridden.

143
00:18:28,048 --> 00:18:31,469
And then he went, and then he sort of cried in front of Dzongtsey Khyentsey.

144
00:18:32,129 --> 00:18:35,010
And Khentsey Rinpoche looked at him and said, why are you crying?

145
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:36,450
He said, well, now,

146
00:18:37,107 --> 00:18:44,151
we all came to no land, came outside of Tibet.

147
00:18:45,852 --> 00:18:51,075
And many lamas passed away, and now you are in this situation.

148
00:18:52,215 --> 00:18:56,698
And I feel that now there is no hope for Tibetan Buddhism or Buddha Dharma.

149
00:18:58,078 --> 00:19:06,383
And Dzongtsey Khyentsey Choejey told him that, don't worry, I heard Dilgo Khyentsey Rinpoche made it to Bhutan, he will take care of the Dharma.

150
00:19:08,246 --> 00:19:09,746
So Dzongtsey Khyentsey told him that.

151
00:19:10,646 --> 00:19:21,548
So when this guy told Khentsey Rinpoche this story, then Khentsey Rinpoche realized that Dzongtsey Khyentsey Rinpoche was put fully trust or hope on him.

152
00:19:22,969 --> 00:19:26,569
Then he started taking medicine and then he got better.

153
00:19:26,589 --> 00:19:33,250
I think then onwards he started non-stop giving teachings till he died.

154
00:19:35,091 --> 00:19:36,131
Non-stop giving teachings.

155
00:19:37,375 --> 00:19:54,560
And I think we can say that nowadays in this world, thanks to Khyentse Rinpoche and like Khyentse Rinpoche, that we still, in the Nyingma Kagyu tradition, we still have the lineages, unbroken lineages from Tibet.

156
00:19:55,760 --> 00:20:02,062
So that we can still enjoy these teachings and all that.

157
00:20:06,255 --> 00:20:08,376
So I'm trying to find what to say because there's only one.

158
00:20:10,998 --> 00:20:14,040
So I'm trying to describe Lama.

159
00:20:17,301 --> 00:20:17,902
So like that.

160
00:20:18,002 --> 00:20:28,548
So when you see really like a great master like many of these Tibetan great masters who came from Tibet are like that.

161
00:20:29,208 --> 00:20:29,929
Khentsey Rinpoche.

162
00:20:30,169 --> 00:20:32,890
I'm talking about Khentsey Rinpoche because I'm more close to Rinpoche.

163
00:20:33,311 --> 00:20:34,451
And I know about Rinpoche.

164
00:20:34,892 --> 00:20:35,612
So many of them.

165
00:20:36,233 --> 00:20:38,914
such a great master.

166
00:20:40,294 --> 00:20:54,318
So you spend time with him and you be with him and then somehow you somehow feel kind of natural devotion.

167
00:20:55,638 --> 00:21:03,020
In my case, first a kind loving grandfather and slowly

168
00:21:03,674 --> 00:21:07,317
turn into my spiritual teacher, Transakshin.

169
00:21:09,238 --> 00:21:16,664
